/T (Directory listing is a web server misconfiguration that displays the contents of a folder like a file browser when no index page exists. The /old folder on the server had directory listing enabled, exposing a database backup file to anyone who visited that URL. I had already found this folder during my initial recon from the robots.txt file, which listed it as a disallowed path. )
/E (Directory listing is a web server misconfiguration that displays the contents of a folder like a file browser when no index page exists. The /old folder on the server had directory listing enabled, exposing a database backup file to anyone who visited that URL. I had already found this folder during my initial recon from the robots.txt file, which listed it as a disallowed path. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
